    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324">

                <pb facs="0497" n="457" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg457"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1534.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-08-31"><hi rendition="#italic">
                                August,</hi> 31, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> It is desirable that a decision in the case
                    of insurgent’s property in England, for which suit has been brought on behalf of
                    this government, especially that of the cotton at Liverpool, should be postponed
                    until the Hon. Caleb Cushing can reach that country, for which he will soon
                    embark, for the purpose of attending to the public interests involved. You will
                    consequently cause this wish to be made known to the United States counsel.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
